 * field element (a `bigint`). To encrypt a byte array (e.g. a 32-byte seed),
 * the caller must first convert it to a field element interpretation or encrypt
 * multiple elements (one per 32-byte chunk, with each chunk treated as a LE
 * integer and reduced modulo p if necessary).
