 *
 * @remarks
 * ## Caching Strategy
 *
 * - **No deps**: a singleton `cachedDefaultChallengePowersFunction` is created on
 *   first call and returned on all subsequent calls.
 * - **Custom `modMul`**: a `WeakMap` keyed by `modMul` reference is consulted
 *   first; if absent a new function is created and stored in the map. This
 *   allows garbage collection of custom functions when their `modMul` key is
 *   collected.
 *
 * ## Performance
 *
 * The returned function uses O(maxPower) field multiplications — the minimum
 * possible for generating all powers 1 through maxPower.
 *
 * @public
 *
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * // Default usage (most common)
 * const computePowers = getChallengePowersFunction();
 * const challenge = getFiatShamirChallengeGeneratorFunction()(transcript);
 * const powers = computePowers(challenge, 9); // [1, c, c^2, ..., c^9]
 * ```
 *
 * @example
 * ```typescript
 * // With a custom modular multiplication function (e.g. for testing)
 * import { getChallengePowersFunction } from './challenges';
 * const powers = getChallengePowersFunction({ modMul: myModMul })(challenge, 5);
 * ```
 *
 * @see {@link ChallengePowersFunction}
 * @see {@link ChallengePowersDeps}
 */
